stall a package that implements the `NpmParserModule` interface:"},"799":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-80","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#npm-package-parser","content":"When both `parseFile` and `parseStream` are exported, Struktur prefers `parseFile` for file inputs (zero-copy) and `parseStream` for buffer or stdin inputs. A temp file is created as a fallback if needed."},"800":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-81","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#npm-package-parser","content":"Register it:"},"801":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-82","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#file-based","content":"The `FILE_PATH` placeholder is replaced with the actual file path at runtime. For buffer inputs, a temp file is created automatically."},"802":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-83","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#file-based","content":"`FILE_PATH` must appear in the command string — an error is thrown if it is missing."},"803":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-84","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#file-based","content":"The command must write `SerializedArtifact[]` JSON to stdout."},"804":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-85","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#stdin-based","content":"File contents are piped to the command's stdin."},"805":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-86","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#stdin-based","content":"The command must write `SerializedArtifact[]` JSON to stdout. Plain text output will fail validation."},"806":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-87","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parser-resolution-order","content":"For any input, parsers are resolved in this order:"},"807":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-88","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parser-resolution-order","content":"`--parser <pkg>` flag on the CLI — always wins, bypasses all config"},"808":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-89","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parser-resolution-order","content":"Parser configured for the detected MIME type (`config parsers add`)"},"809":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-90","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parser-resolution-order","content":"Built-in parser (PDF, text/\\*, image/\\*, JSON)"},"810":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-91","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parser-resolution-order","content":"Error with a suggestion to use `config parsers add`"},"811":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-92","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#ad-hoc-parser-override","content":"Use `--parser` to override the configured parser for a single run without changing config:"},"812":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-93","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#parseinput-options","content":"The primary SDK function for loading input into artifacts. Handles MIME detection and parser resolution automatically."},"813":{"id":"/docs/exp