i-Step Strategies"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"How smart validation works"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Opting into strict validation"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"See also"},"1410":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Without in-loop validation, you get JSON that may or may not match your schema. You then have to write error handling, decide whether to retry, and figure out how to feed errors back."},"1411":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Struktur does all of this for you."},"1412":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Send the extraction prompt to the LLM."},"1413":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Validate the response with Ajv against the schema."},"1414":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If valid: return it."},"1415":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If invalid: serialize the Ajv error array into an XML block, append it to the message thread as a user message, go to step 1."},"1416":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"After `maxAttempts` (default 3): throw."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"The model sees its own mistake and a structured description of it. This self-correction loop is why most extractions converge within 2 attempts."},"1418":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Well-constrained schemas fail less often. Tips:"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Always use `additionalProperties: false`."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `required` arrays explicitly."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Prefer `enum` for categorical fields."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `format` (e.g., `date`, `email`) only when you need it — it adds validation surface."},"1423":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#observing-retries-with-events","content":"Use the `onMessage` event to see when retries happen:"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#smart-validation-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"When using parallel or sequential strategies, your data might be split across multiple chunks. For example, an invoice's price might appear on page 1, while the vendor name appears on page 5. If both fields are `required` in your schema, validating intermediate results would fail unnecessarily."},"1425":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Type errors** (`string` vs `number`) → Retry immediately"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Format errors** (invalid email) → Retry immediately"},"1428":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Required field errors** → Allowed during intermediate steps"},"1429":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**All constraints** → Enforced on final validation"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"This means the model can extract partial data without pressure to hallucinate missing required fields. The final validation ensures all required fields are present before returning."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Disable smart validation with the `strict` flag:"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Use `strict: true` when:"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-32","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You know each chunk contains complete data"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-33","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You want early failure on missing fields"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-34","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You're debugging extraction issues"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-35","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Extraction Pipeline — where validation fits"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-36","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"Events & Observability — the events API"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-37","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Artifact Format — schema format"},"1439":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"What is Struktur?","breadcrumbs":["Struktur"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"1440":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Struktur is a structured data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated JSON using LLMs."},"1441":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Why Struktur?"},"1442":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Why not managed APIs?"},"1443":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"Why not a plain LLM SDK call?"},"1444":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"Design philosophy"},"1445":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Trade-offs"},"1446":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"A 10-second demo"},"1447":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"What Struktur is NOT"},"1448":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"Who is it for?"},"1449":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-are-strategies","content":"What are Strategies?"},"1450":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#built-in-strategies","content":"Built-in strategies"},"1451":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#quick-navigation","content":"Quick navigation"},"1452":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Struktur is a structured data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated, schema-typed JSON. It operates on JSON-based artifact DTOs, chunks them by token budgets, runs extraction strategies, validates results with Ajv, and merges or deduplicates outputs where needed."},"1453":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Large document batches arrive with data locked in semi-structured text. Invoices need to flow into spreadsheets. Product datasheets need to become database rows. The tooling exists, but the orchestration overhead is disproportionate to the extraction task itself."},"1454":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Managed APIs charge per page, impose schema constraints, and require document uploads to external infrastructure. LLM SDKs provide raw model access but leave you to write chunking, validation, retries, and merging every time."},"1455":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Struktur fills the gap: a focused extraction engine that handles the orchestration so you can focus on the output."},"1456":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Limitation"},"1457":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Impact"},"1458":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Per-page pricing"},"1459":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Does not scale for large batches"},"1460":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Schema constraints"},"1461":{"id":"/docs-21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"You work within their data model"},"1462":{"id":"/docs-22","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Document upload"},"1463":{"id":"/docs-23","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Non-starter for confidential workloads"},"1464":{"id":"/docs-24","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Black-box behavior"},"1465":{"id":"/docs-25","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Debugging extraction failures is opaque"},"1466":{"id":"/docs-26","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"A single `generateText()` call gives you:"},"1467":{"id":"/docs-27","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No chunking for large documents"},"1468":{"id":"/docs-28","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No retries on schema validation failure"},"1469":{"id":"/docs-29","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No merging of multi-chunk results"},"1470":{"id":"/docs-30","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No typed output inferred from your schema"},"1471":{"id":"/docs-31","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"You write the same orchestration boilerplate every time. Struktur packages that orchestration into tested, configurable strategies."},"1472":{"id":"/docs-32","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Narrow scope, intentionally.** Struktur does extraction only. No parsing. No streaming. No general-purpose LLM orchestration. This focus keeps the API small and the behavior predictable."},"1473":{"id":"/docs-33","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Shell-composable by default.** Reads stdin, writes stdout, speaks JSON. Integrates with `jq`, `find`, `curl`, and any tool in your pipeline."},"1474":{"id":"/docs-34","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Strategy-first.** Different documents need different approaches. A single-page invoice needs simple extraction. A 100-page catalog with duplicate products needs parallel extraction with deduplication. Strategies encode these patterns."},"1475":{"id":"/docs-35","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Validation in the loop.** Errors go back to the model, not to you. The retry loop means most extractions converge within two attempts."},"1476":{"id":"/docs-36","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Schema-first.** You define the shape, Struktur guarantees it."},"1477":{"id":"/docs-37","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Fields shorthand.** Skip the JSON Schema boilerplate with `--fields \"title, price:number, status:enum{draft|live}\"`."},"1478":{"id":"/docs-38","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Trade-off"},"1479":{"id":"/docs-39","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Rationale"},"1480":{"id":"/docs-40","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Requires upstream preprocessing"},"1481":{"id":"/docs-41","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Keeps Struktur focused; use best-of-breed parsers per format"},"1482":{"id":"/docs-42","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Batch-only, no streaming"},"1483":{"id":"/docs-43","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Simpler mental model; input in, JSON out"},"1484":{"id":"/docs-44","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Depends on Vercel AI SDK providers"},"1485":{"id":"/docs-45","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"OpenAI, Anthropic, Google supported; self-hosted models need OpenAI-compatible API"},"1486":{"id":"/docs-46","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Token costs depend on strategy"},"1487":{"id":"/docs-47","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"`doublePass` costs more than `simple`; know your rates"},"1488":{"id":"/docs-48","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"Expected output:"},"1489":{"id":"/docs-49","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a general document conversion tool.** It parses files for extraction purposes, not for format conversion. It does not produce formatted output from documents."},"1490":{"id":"/docs-50","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a managed API.** It runs locally and calls your provider directly."},"1491":{"id":"/docs-51","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It does not stream.** Input in, JSON out."},"1492":{"id":"/docs-52","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a general LLM orchestration framework.**"},"1493":{"id":"/docs-53","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"For the full mental model, see The Extraction Pipeline."},"1494":{"id":"/docs-54","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"**CLI users** — data engineers, analysts, shell pipeline builders — use Struktur for one-off extractions, batch pro